{
 "result": "fibmod.py is a fast body: it reduces each n mod the Pisano period 2(P+1), then uses a two-level table of F(iB) and F(iB-1) with B=2^16, so each query costs two multiplications and a lookup. It passed the sample input (30,005 lines, byte-identical output) and the sanity check (10 gives 55). The assay registered a baseline of 13.4913 with 7.1% noise. Further gains look marginal relative to the noise and the energy cost of more steps, so I am stopping here.",
